# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Virtual environment
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Environment secrets. `.env.*` plus an explicit allow for the template covers
# every variant, including `.env.production` and `.env.dev`. It replaced
# `.env.local` / `.env.*.local`, which matched neither of those two.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Plaintext key scratch files. `docs/` below already covers docs/KEYS.MD, but
# only incidentally -- the same file one directory up was committable. Nothing
# in the harness reads these; keys reach the code through .env only.
KEYS.md
KEYS.MD
keys.md
SECRETS.md
secrets.md

# Docs, reviews, and research (not version-controlled going forward)
docs/
reviews/
research/

# Local runtime data (agent run transcripts, bridge SQLite database)
logs/
*.sqlite3

# CodeGraph local index (machine-specific, rebuildable via `codegraph init`)
.codegraph/

# Vendored agent skills (machine-local tooling, re-installable). Previously this
# held an orphaned gitlink: `.agents/skills/blueprint` was committed at mode
# 160000 while no .gitmodules ever existed, so a clone got an empty directory and
# `git submodule foreach` failed outright -- which broke CI checkout the moment
# persist-credentials: false made it run that cleanup. See RAID I20.
.agents/

